### META
directory_path: services
description: DINS service definitions - each subdirectory contains a complete service definition per PART 9
created: 2025-11-29
modified: 2025-11-29
status: active

### STRUCTURE
Each service directory MUST contain:
- service.yaml | Service descriptor (name, type, image, runtime config)
- src/ | Program code (if locally managed)
- config/ | Default configuration templates (non-secret)
- docs/ | Service-specific documentation
- tests/ | Service-specific tests
- Dockerfile | (optional) for local builds

### SERVICE_TYPES
core | Core DINS/DINSER infrastructure services
agent | AI/LLM agent services
frontend | User-facing frontends
storage | Storage services (DRNAS, etc.)
vpn | VPN/mesh services (Tailscale, etc.)
stt | Speech-to-text services
tts | Text-to-speech services
gateway | Web gateways and proxies

### BUILD_MODES (per PART 9.3)
local-build | Build from local files in service directory
remote-build | Build from temporary downloaded files (git clone)
prebuilt | Use prebuilt image from registry

### DIRECTORIES
_example/ | Example service template (not deployable)

### LIFECYCLE
1. Create service directory with structure above
2. Define service.yaml descriptor
3. dinser service build <name> to build image
4. dinser service deploy <name> to deploy to swarm
5. dinser service status <name> to check status
